  "rejections": [
    {
      "decision_id": "primary_photo_species_70916f96d37c2216",
      "reason": "Reject the split as an indivisible decision after independently checking all 18 assignments. The identity assignments for `in vitro` and `in_vitro` do not themselves introduce a new label, but moving `in_vitro_cells (purified lipofuscin granules)` to `non-biological/computational context` is unsupported: purified lipofuscin granules are explicitly biological material, not a computational or non-biological system. The policy forbids asserting a system identity absent from the raw value. Because an accepted split must assign every raw value correctly and cannot be partially rewritten during adjudication, the whole decision must be rejected and returned for a less-specific acellular/biological-system disposition."
    },
    {
      "decision_id": "primary_photo_species_d1c4cef652d78434",
      "reason": "Reject the split as an indivisible decision after independently checking all 13 assignments. The row `animal_in_vivo (passive transfer ex vivo exposure)` explicitly contains both an animal-in-vivo scope and an ex-vivo exposure component, yet the proposal assigns it only to `animal in vivo`. That erases an explicit experimental-system dimension protected by policy; it needs a mixed or combined literal child. Since adjudication cannot rewrite one assignment inside an exhaustive split, the entire decision must be rejected pending correction."
    }
  ],
